  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8e03584264278974592ae603cbd2455f, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HintText
  HintIndex: 0
  FadeTime: 0.2
  VisibleTime: 3
  Hints:
  - Use the tactical lens to get a glimpse into an enemy's behavior
  - Units generally fight better close to friends
  - If an enemy is avoiding combat, they may have a strategic goal you can't see.
    Beware traps
  - Giving gifts can help you build support and recruit new allies
  - Ships sell rare or exotic goods you won't find elsewhere
  - Different ships from various places will dock at different times. You never know
    what you'll find at the docks
  - As you visit and buy from ships, the crew will come to trust you- and may even
    sell you secret smuggled goods
  - The blacksmith can repair damaged weapons
  - Riding units cover great distances but are hindered by sand and forest
  - Flying units are vulnerable to archers
  - Many truncheons are effective against armor or riders, they may be more useful
    than they seem
  - There are four types of magic, each with various strengths
  - Transcendent magic does little damage but has powerful effects on living beings
    that can change the tide of battle
  - Cosmic magic is expensive and fragile, but can devastate enemies
  _textComponent: {fileID: 2047517348927099354}
